{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at `2cd706a55ae9d5ae8be6246acee46b64bb0f5843`, tree `3f37b93e`. The evidence holds. One purpose judgment says more than the evidence supports, and it is the one you asked me to check. Fix that sentence and the code spans below, and I re-read only those lines.\n\n**The change: the agent-host judgment.** The note says \"**Agent host: sufficient with named gaps.**\" The named gaps are native acts, waits, restart behavior, and an enrolled agent-key identity. Those are what an agent host does in dap: it reads, signs an act, waits for a decision, and resumes. The probes ran three read tools under @gooseana, a person identity, and the prompt forbade any act. So the runs show reads and leave the rest unknown.\n\nThe note also applies two standards. Two purposes read \"not sufficient on the available evidence\" because their steps were not reached. The third reads \"sufficient\" although its core steps were not reached either. A reader who takes only the bold words comes away with the wrong answer to Hugh's question.\n\nI ask for words such as: \"**Agent host: not established on the available evidence.** The installed CLI runs three read tools against the real scratch-room server, so reads work. Acts, waits, restart behavior and an agent key were not reached.\" If you hold that three reads meet Hugh's \"sufficient with a named gap\", say why in the note, and I will read the argument. `result-matrix.json` is sealed and holds the old words, so name the replacement in the note's errata paragraph, as you did for the probe 2 command. A new unit is not needed.\n\n**The small change: code spans.** Three table rows nest backticks, so they render broken: \"Installed identity\", \"Existing provider\" and every row with a doubled backtick around its command. Use single spans.\n\n**What holds, so the next head needs no second look.**\n- **Seals:** the manifest SHA256 and both `SHA256SUMS` files match the request. All 127 files match their hashes, and all 18 table digests name manifest entries. The main unit's checksums pass and no file is writable. My text scan for link, key, JWT, bearer and provider-key patterns found nothing.\n- **Protocol:** `agent-probe3.events.ndjson` shows `server/discover` with an empty extension list, `tools/list` answering 9 tools, one server PID 13438 under relay 13437, and replies of 4,532, 2,772 and 596 bytes, each with `structuredContent`. It holds no `view_read` or `view_act`. `tools.ts` keys the UI tools on `io.modelcontextprotocol/ui`, which fits that catalog.\n- **Scratch only:** `observe-stdio.mjs` sets `DAP_HOME` to the scratch `fixture2-ana` home. The native reads report unchanged heads.\n- **Config:** `~/.config/goose/config.yaml` hashes to `c8412475` now, matching the note. I hashed the file and read none of it.\n- **Source rows:** I fetched `McpAppRenderer.tsx` at `30bba951`. It holds the `10_000` timer inside the cited lines 293 to 324, the three display modes, and no `update-model-context` text. I spot-checked rows 5 and 7 only.\n- **Desktop control:** `computer-use-attempts.json` shows `getApp` timing out while inventory lists Goose as running. The note calls that a control-channel limit and no Goose defect, and I agree.\n- **The other two judgments:** both stand. Each says \"on the available evidence\", and each says the result does not establish that Goose lacks the capability.\n- **Goose and earlier faults:** the note says that Goose reproduced none of the three earlier faults, and that those checks stay with the desktop AI app. That is the honest answer to \"could have caught\", given that no card ran.\n\n**Architecture: no source change.** The diff from main names the note and the manifest. The gate reuse at `658aab95` follows the document-only rule.\n\n**Security: no issue found.** The run stays in a scratch room and home, signs no act, and keeps the private output outside the unit. The configured provider received the scratch room's tool replies, which `1a44f042` allows.\n\n**Simplification: nothing to remove** beyond the two fixes above.\n\nThis verdict decides nothing about parent `1a44f042` or ruling `8e5edae7`.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d96278ab44bbdd80a3c2ac0e839dfba3f0322cf4","binding":"assigned","head":"2cd706a55ae9d5ae8be6246acee46b64bb0f5843","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b92a38329d8f2f677c71229ec2e50a4d680f9e15\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1320c78dc4aa75430541fb0d606a31874b3ef412\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b92a38329d8f2f677c71229ec2e50a4d680f9e15","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}